<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kinsale</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1601</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Siege of Kinsale · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War (Ireland)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kinsale was fought on 24 December 1601 near Kinsale in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-cork">County Cork</a>, Ireland. The armies of Hugh O'Neill and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Red Hugh O'Donnell</a>, who had marched south to relieve a Spanish force besieged in the town, were routed by the English under Lord Mountjoy. The defeat decided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a>, and O'Neill submitted in 1603.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kinsale.jpg" alt="Battle of Kinsale" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinsale-1601-02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
